s":[{"surface":"தேற்றா","parts":[{"text":"தேற்றா","lemma":"தேற்று","gloss":"unclear"}],"gloss":"simple"},{"surface":"புன்","parts":[{"text":"புன்","lemma":"புன்","gloss":"humble"}],"gloss":"humble"},{"surface":"சொல்","parts":[{"text":"சொல்","lemma":"சொல்","gloss":"words"}],"gloss":"words"},{"surface":"நோற்றிசின்","parts":[{"text":"நோற்றிசின்","lemma":"நோல்","gloss":"please bear with"}],"gloss":"please bear with"},{"surface":"பெரும","parts":[{"text":"பெரும","lemma":"பெரும","gloss":"O great lord"}],"gloss":"O great lord"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"விடுத்தனென்","parts":[{"text":"விடுத்தனென்","lemma":"விடு","gloss":"I have left"}],"gloss":"I have left"},{"surface":"வெலீஇயர்","parts":[{"text":"வெலீஇயர்","lemma":"வெல்","gloss":"may it conquer"}],"gloss":"may it conquer"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"வேலே","parts":[{"text":"வேலே","lemma":"வேல்","gloss":"spear indeed"}],"gloss":"spear indeed"},{"surface":"அடுக்கத்து","parts":[{"text":"அடுக்கத்து","lemma":"அடுக்கம்","gloss":"mountain range"}],"gloss":"on the mountain range"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அரும்பு","parts":[{"text":"அரும்பு","lemma":"அரும்பு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அற","parts":[{"text":"அற","lemma":"அற","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மலர்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"மலர்ந்த","lemma":"மலர்ந்த","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கருங்கால்","parts":[{"text":"கருங்கால்","lemma":"கருங்கால்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேங்கை","parts":[{"text":"வேங்கை","lemma":"வேங்கை","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"மா","parts":[{"text":"மா","lemma":"மா","gloss":"dark"}],"gloss":"dark"},{"surface":"தகட்டு","parts":[{"text":"தகட்டு","lemma":"தகடு","gloss":"petal"}],"gloss":"petaled"},{"surface":"ஒள்","parts":[{"text":"ஒள்","lemma":"ஒள்","gloss":"bright"}],"gloss":"bright"},{"surface":"வீ","parts":[{"text":"வீ","lemma":"வீ","gloss":"flowers"}],"gloss":"flowers"},{"surface":"தாய","parts":[{"text":"தாய","lemma":"தாய்","gloss":"scattered"}],"gloss":"scattered over"},{"surface":"துறுகல்","parts":[{"text":"துறுகல்","lemma":"துறுகல்","gloss":"boulder"}],"gloss":"boulder"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இரும்","parts":[{"text":"இரும்","lemma":"இரும்","gloss":"big"}],"gloss":"big"},{"surface":"புலி","parts":[{"text":"புலி","lemma":"புலி","gloss":"tiger"}],"gloss":"tiger's"},{"surface":"வரி","parts":[{"text":"வரி","lemma":"வரி","gloss":"striped"}],"gloss":"striped"},{"surface":"புறம்","parts":[{"text":"புறம்","lemma":"புறம்","gloss":"back"}],"gloss":"back"},{"surface":"கடுக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"கடுக்கும்","lemma":"கடு","gloss":"resembling"}],"gloss":"resembling"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருங்கல்","parts":[{"text":"பெருங்கல்","lemma":"பெருங்கல்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வைப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"வைப்பின்","lemma":"வைப்பின்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாடுகிழ","parts":[{"text":"நாடுகிழ","lemma":"நாடுகிழ","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வோயே","parts":[{"text":"வோயே","lemma":"வோயே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"When hunters chase in the Ixora forest / the wild bull, not finding a hiding place, / makes sapphires rise and scattered gold glitter / as it rushes swiftly on the high mountain slopes. / Possessing the great fame of established victory, / in the ancient town named after two sides, / which helped you with wealth piled up in many crores, / hear now of the ruin of Araiyam of long standing! / Your father's inheritance fully attained, / O tiger-chasing Lord of the flourishing chaplet, / one among your people, of wisdom like yours, / despised the praised poem of Kazhāttalai, / and the result of that contempt, O lord of the swift chariot, / was that the ancient lineage of Evvi perished. And so, / when I said, 'These are the daughters of generous Pāri,' / please bear with my simple, humble words, O great lord! / I have left. May your spear conquer! O lord of the country / of great mountain regions, where on the slopes / the Kino tree, blossomed fully without buds, / has its bright flowers with dark petals scattered over the boulder, / resembling the striped back of a great tiger!","translation":"O Lord of the country of great mountain regions! On your slopes, the Kino tree has blossomed so fully that not a single bud remains; its bright, dark-petaled flowers scatter over the boulders, making them look like the striped backs of great tigers. I have left now. May your spear always be victorious!\nWhen hunters chase a wild bull in the Ixora forest, it finds no hiding place and rushes swiftly down the high mountain slopes, kicking up sapphires and scattering glittering gold. You rule the ancient, awe-inspiring town named after two sides, which once aided you with wealth piled up in many crores. Hear now of the ruin of Araiyam, which stood for so long!\nA chief among your ancestors, possessing wisdom like yours, attained his father's inheritance and wore a flourishing chaplet. He was the great tiger-chasing Lord. Yet, he despised the praised poem of the poet Kazhāttalai. The result of that contempt, O lord of the swift chariot, was that the ancient lineage of Evvi perished.\nTherefore, O great lord, please bear with my simple, humble words when I brought them and said, 'These are the daughters of the generous Pāri!'","modern":"வெட்சி நிறைந்த காட்டில் வேட்டைக்காரர்கள் துரத்த, ஒளிந்துகொள்ள இடம் தேடாத காட்டு எருது, நீல மணிகளும் பொன்னும் சிதறி மின்னும்படி உயர்ந்த மலைச்சரிவுகளில் வேகமாக ஓடும். வெற்றி பொருந்திய புகழுடன் விளங்கும், இரு பிரிவுகளாகப் பெயர்பெற்ற பழமையான ஊரில், பல கோடிப் பொருள்களை உங்களுக்கு உதவியாகக் கொண்ட அரையத்தின் அழிவைப் பற்றி இப்போது கேட்பாயாக! உன் தந்தையின் அரசை முழுமையாகப் பெற்று, தழைத்த மாலையை அணிந்த, புலியை விரட்டிய வேளிர் குலத் தலைவனே! உன்னைப் போன்ற அறிவுடைய உன் முன்னோர்களில் ஒருவன், புகழ் பெற்ற கவிஞரான கழாத்தலையாரின் பாடலை இகழ்ந்தான். அவ்வாறு இகழ்ந்ததன் பயனாக, தேர் நடத்தும் தலைவனே, வள்ளல் எவ்வியின் தொன்மையான குடி அழிந்துபோனது. அதனால், 'இவர்கள் கொடைத்திறன் மிக்க பாரியின் மகளிர்கள்' என்று நான் கூறிய எளிய சொற்களைப் பொறுத்துக் கொள்வாயாக, பெருமானே! நான் விடைபெறுகிறேன், உன் வேல் வெல்வதாக! மலைச்சரிவுகளில் அரும்புகள் இன்றி முழுமையாக மலர்ந்த வேங்கை மரத்தின் பொன்னிற மலர்கள் பாறைகளின் மேல் உதிர்ந்து கிடப்பது, பெரிய புலியின் வரி விழுந்த முதுகைப் போலத் தோன்றும் பெரிய மலைநாட்டின் தலைவனே!","explanation":"The poet Kapilar is addressing the chieftain Iruṅkōvēḷ, presenting the daughters of his deceased friend, the generous patron Pāri, and asking him to marry them. When Iruṅkōvēḷ hesitates or refuses, Kapilar warns him by recalling a historical event: an ancestor of Iruṅkōvēḷ once insulted the poet Kazhāttalai, which led to the complete destruction of the ancient lineage of Evvi and the ruin of the city of Araiyam. Kapilar uses this cautionary tale to emphasize that disrespecting poets and refusing righteous requests brings ruin to great dynasties. The poem is set in the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai (praise of a patron's lineage and power) with elements of Kuriñci (mountain landscape). The vivid imagery of the mountain slopes, where fallen yellow Vēṅkai flowers on dark boulders resemble striped tigers, reflects both the natural wealth of the chieftain's land and the underlying danger of his pride. Key words like 'புலிகடி மாஅல்' (tiger-chasing lord) and 'இகழ்ந்ததன் பயனே' (the consequence of contempt) highlight the theme of ancestral pride and the peril of arrogance.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}